@startuml
!theme plain
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
title A2A QR / Deep Link Payment Architecture — Synthetic HLD
actor Payer
component "Merchant Checkout\n(Web / POS / Mobile)" as Checkout
component "Merchant Backend" as Merchant
package "A2A Payment Platform" {
 component "Merchant API Gateway" as Gateway
 component "Payment Orchestrator" as Orch
 component "Initiation Adapter" as Adapter
 component "Verified Callback Inbox" as Inbox
 component "Recovery Worker" as Recovery
 component "Merchant Webhook Outbox" as Outbox
 component "Reconciliation" as Recon
 database "Intent / Attempt Store" as DB
}
cloud "External Payment Provider" as Provider
component "Payer Banking App" as App
Payer --> Checkout : start A2A checkout
Checkout --> Merchant : confirm order
Merchant --> Gateway : create payment intent
Gateway --> Orch : validate / authorize
Orch --> DB : durable intent and attempt
Orch --> Adapter : provider initiation
Adapter --> Provider : register instruction
Provider --> Adapter : checkout token / link
Adapter --> Orch : opaque initiation data
Orch --> Merchant : return intent and channel URI
Merchant --> Checkout : display QR / open app link
Payer --> App : authorize via QR / deep link
App --> Provider : authorization / outcome
Provider ..> Inbox : verified status event
Inbox --> DB : guarded state transition
Inbox --> Outbox : durable merchant event
Outbox ..> Merchant : webhook (retries independent)
Recovery ..> Provider : query UNKNOWN outcomes
Recovery --> DB : reconcile local state
Recon ..> Provider : match provider status/report
note bottom of Checkout
Browser return and QR scan do not confirm payment success.
Only verified provider evidence updates financial status.
end note
@enduml